{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1791045549,"nonce":"1cAzbb386R7uDD8VS09eKvQ0DPY=","title":"for-in over an abstract iterates its underlying value as an array","message":"Rows: Issue4705, Issue7659, Issue7661.\n\nir/mir/stmt/for_in.rs `lower_for_in_loop` has no TypeKind::Abstract case: an abstract (kind 9) is in\nneither the iterator-protocol list nor the anon branch and falls to `lower_for_in_over_array`, which\nreads the underlying value as a HaxeArray. The abstract's own `iterator()` (or its hasNext/next) is\nnever called; Haxe prefers `iterator()` over @:arrayAccess+length. With an inline `new Abstract(..)`\nthe HIR type has already decayed to the underlying anon, so a check on `iter_expr.ty` alone misses it.\nRelated: d925c9c, 09019f0 (the hasNext/next rewrite was removed for looping forever).","files":null}]}